    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 105,
        "text": "Hi Li, how was your visit to the new museum exhibition? I heard it's about ancient Chinese inventions.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "93432f962002dfb4ef24b8c29210693611529a3b55304f402a2885f4e049b181",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 109,
        "sourceEnd": 300,
        "text": "Oh, it was fascinating! Although I'm not usually a museum person, I really enjoyed it. The exhibition focuses on the Four Great Inventions, but it also includes some lesser-known discoveries.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "b640bee2189aa2f59fa781637bc7583c5dadf7a69c62b5b0efffefd5ce5d8130",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 304,
        "sourceEnd": 322,
        "text": "Really? Like what?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a56579205d65f2faf48188775c2443845efa26f7d6e822f43acab94198ec4625",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 326,
        "sourceEnd": 549,
        "text": "Well, for example, the seismoscope, which was invented by Zhang Heng in the Han Dynasty. It's a bronze vessel with dragons and toads, and it can detect earthquakes. Even though it's ancient, the design is incredibly clever.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "4493983ccfaf5aced8cfca8f02e90cfffb0359a0557d11c11e45bc7affb95bb2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 553,
        "sourceEnd": 616,
        "text": "That sounds impressive. Did they have any interactive displays?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "5ad9b6b08bf73afd4577c8549685c311a7b3d63565718eb99ac0a09b0fc11058",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 620,
        "sourceEnd": 804,
        "text": "Yes, they did. There was a section where you could try to operate a replica of the seismoscope. It was quite challenging, but fun. Also, they had a hologram showing how paper was made.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "38e926daba2faf73180d5d8fa12a6f30b386700322bbea240438197d7c54a42c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 808,
        "sourceEnd": 875,
        "text": "I see. What about the compass? I've always been curious about that.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "61146ae23874b320602adbf3d2915a4601b57859640967d6887006bacf19e594",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 879,
        "sourceEnd": 1096,
        "text": "The compass was originally used for divination, not navigation. That's something I didn't know before. The exhibition explained that the first compasses were made of lodestone, which is a naturally magnetized mineral.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "4a5509f0d9e5b21010237e0d23ee7699ace95a4e7325f8f64eb59b00516dde5a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1100,
        "sourceEnd": 1160,
        "text": "Interesting. So when did they start using it for navigation?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "f45a54deb814c2833ec3d63cc293479466c8437fb48504ec6b684d1dc340a41c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1164,
        "sourceEnd": 1361,
        "text": "According to the display, it was during the Song Dynasty that compasses were first used for sea navigation. But some historians argue it might have been earlier. The exhibition presents both views.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "f2fbf5049b5fd7afb09c47b625dad315da29359dfa0a36e3f23db58fc5cdeb6b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1365,
        "sourceEnd": 1448,
        "text": "That's good—showing different perspectives. Did you learn anything about gunpowder?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "14b48f63d6a00e092b2d54bfe95857677ee89702c22ff08f14a1f8beb00ea6e3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1452,
        "sourceEnd": 1648,
        "text": "Yes, gunpowder was actually discovered by accident by alchemists who were trying to find an elixir of life. Instead, they created an explosive mixture. The exhibition had a short video about that.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "8d110800964064147b068e144f2dbb8cec307c2567267b359f59bec30618a71b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1652,
        "sourceEnd": 1729,
        "text": "Wow. So the exhibition covers both the successes and the unexpected outcomes.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "f2483df2887e1cbea3d73ae979cf12b9d70b01c89c0bd8c518cf34b6f5c3c427",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1733,
        "sourceEnd": 1993,
        "text": "Exactly. And what I found most interesting was the section on printing. They showed how woodblock printing evolved into movable type, which was a major breakthrough. Although movable type was invented in China, it wasn't widely used until much later in Europe.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "0fd4b71c3381706873051e7d5d19b26fe7409f9a965ea73747cc7152a1d33983",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1997,
        "sourceEnd": 2069,
        "text": "That's a good point. It's amazing how these inventions shaped the world.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "7fe6e19c19cd387ddb09a6f20857693825587df50f98304b046272f57288e21e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 2073,
        "sourceEnd": 2232,
        "text": "Yes, and the exhibition does a great job of connecting the past to the present. For instance, it shows how modern seismographs are based on similar principles.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "9d993acb1ce5c0fe578ef31280fbf7a832de762f1f1741fff0ebbe3b38eb84e7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 2236,
        "sourceEnd": 2289,
        "text": "I'll definitely visit. Thanks for the recommendation!",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "2b6aba1654eddbe131cb265c8304d4422bb8a429c36292e57f15752b3cda258b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 2293,
        "sourceEnd": 2368,
        "text": "You're welcome. I think you'll enjoy it, even if you're not a history buff.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "5eb2aa0ead0f62efaa5387a9701f523a0ef3d412c2d3e9a11cf37ad7303d08c5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
